<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>LLM on Wei's Home</title><link>https://weiguo98.github.io/tags/llm/</link><description>Recent content in LLM on Wei's Home</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><managingEditor>guow1227@gmail.com (Wei Guo)</managingEditor><webMaster>guow1227@gmail.com (Wei Guo)</webMaster><copyright>© 2026 Wei Guo</copyright><lastBuildDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://weiguo98.github.io/tags/llm/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Agent Design: Workflow or Agent?</title><link>https://weiguo98.github.io/blog/agent-workflow-vs-agent/agent-workflow-vs-agent/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>guow1227@gmail.com (Wei Guo)</author><guid>https://weiguo98.github.io/blog/agent-workflow-vs-agent/agent-workflow-vs-agent/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Before building an LLM feature, answer one question first: does this need an agent, or an automated workflow?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;1. Check whether you really need an agent&#10; &lt;div id="1-check-whether-you-really-need-an-agent" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;span&#10; class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#1-check-whether-you-really-need-an-agent" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;/span&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;When people say they want an agent, they often want an &lt;strong&gt;automated workflow&lt;/strong&gt;: the steps are fixed, and only some of them are handed to a model.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;In a workflow, code decides the path. In an agent, the model decides the path. If you can write the path down in advance, build a workflow. It is cheaper, faster, and easier to test and debug.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;An agent is only worth it when you don&amp;rsquo;t know the number or order of steps up front, and the next step depends on intermediate results.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Even with an agent, split big tasks into subtasks, each with clear inputs and outputs.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="admonition relative overflow-hidden rounded-lg border-l-4 my-3 px-4 py-3 shadow-sm" data-type="tip"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold text-inherit"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="flex shrink-0 h-5 w-5 items-center justify-center text-lg"&gt;&lt;span class="relative block icon"&gt;&lt;svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 384 512"&gt;&lt;path fill="currentColor" d="M112.1 454.3c0 6.297 1.816 12.44 5.284 17.69l17.14 25.69c5.25 7.875 17.17 14.28 26.64 14.28h61.67c9.438 0 21.36-6.401 26.61-14.28l17.08-25.68c2.938-4.438 5.348-12.37 5.348-17.7L272 415.1h-160L112.1 454.3zM191.4 .0132C89.44 .3257 16 82.97 16 175.1c0 44.38 16.44 84.84 43.56 115.8c16.53 18.84 42.34 58.23 52.22 91.45c.0313 .25 .0938 .5166 .125 .7823h160.2c.0313-.2656 .0938-.5166 .125-.7823c9.875-33.22 35.69-72.61 52.22-91.45C351.6 260.8 368 220.4 368 175.1C368 78.61 288.9-.2837 191.4 .0132zM192 96.01c-44.13 0-80 35.89-80 79.1C112 184.8 104.8 192 96 192S80 184.8 80 176c0-61.76 50.25-111.1 112-111.1c8.844 0 16 7.159 16 16S200.8 96.01 192 96.01z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="grow"&gt;&#10; Tip&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="admonition-content mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-inherit"&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you can write the path down in advance, make it a workflow.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>